Task: Write tests for ParentLock component

Summary:
Created test suite for the ParentLock component following TDD Red phase.
The tests define the API contract for a hold-for-3-seconds parental lock
mechanism using Phaser input events. ParentLock registers pointerdown,
pointerup, and pointerout listeners on a target game object, starts a
timer on pointerdown, fires onSuccess when the timer completes, and
fires onFailure (canceling the timer) when the pointer is released or
leaves the target before the hold duration elapses.

Files Created:
- src/__tests__/components/ParentLock.test.ts (209 lines, 18 test cases)

Test Structure (4 describe blocks):
1. constructor: Verifies pointerdown/pointerup/pointerout listeners
   are registered on the target (3 tests)
2. hold detection: Tests timer starts with 3000ms default, custom
   holdDuration, and onSuccess fires on completion (3 tests)
3. reset on release before 3s: Tests pointerup/pointerout cancel timer,
   fire onFailure, no onSuccess, and no failure without active hold (7 tests)
4. destroy(): Tests listener removal, timer cancellation, and no-error
   when no timer active (5 tests)

Mock Strategy:
- MockTarget: Event emitter with on/off/emit methods, captures callbacks
  for invocation via emit()
- MockScene: Contains time.delayedCall which captures the timer callback
  and returns a MockTimerEvent with remove()
- MockFn type alias: ReturnType<typeof vi.fn> for consistent typing
- as never casts used for mock objects passed to ParentLock constructor

